# The wire tile for a row three blocks deep: the west-east arm along the middle
# row (z = 1), the north-south arm down the middle column (x = 2), so a hop
# along the row costs five dust steps and one across it three. A repeater goes
# in the arm the signal enters by, as in the wire tile; entering from the north
# or south, that arm is the centre itself, so a straight carries it there and a
# turn in the arm it leaves by, next to that port.
tile wire_s
size 5 4 3
port W io 0 1 1
port E io 4 1 1
port N io 2 1 0
port S io 2 1 2

legend
  C minecraft:glass
  c minecraft:redstone_wire
  W minecraft:glass if W
  w minecraft:redstone_wire if W
  E minecraft:glass if E
  e minecraft:redstone_wire if E
  N minecraft:glass if N
  n minecraft:redstone_wire if N
  S minecraft:glass if S
  s minecraft:redstone_wire if S

layer 0
  ..N..
  WWCEE
  ..S..
layer 1
  ..n..
  wwcee
  ..s..
